 --   Failure at any step (fix 3, 2026-10-16): the member stays in the harbor, is NOT put back into a party (the ship
 --   may already have a new crew; they can board again), and must RE-CLAIM their save session before playing on.
 --   If the re-claim fails they are disconnected with a message, so they rejoin and load their saved progress fresh.
+--
+-- Live-activation safeguards (2026-10-16):
+--   * Every launch carries a TICKET from HarborDepartures. When the harbor gives up on a launch (timeout) it cancels
+--     the ticket; the launch checks it before every irreversible step (reserve, manifest, teleport) and, once
+--     cancelled, recovers its crew instead of teleporting them. A timed-out launch can never teleport an old crew.
+--   * Every save-adapter call (handoff, reclaim) is protected: an exception counts as a failure, so the player is
+--     recovered (re-claim, or disconnect to rejoin) and never left InTransit.
+--   * A teleport that was requested but never completed (no TeleportInitFailed, player still here) is recovered by a
+--     watchdog after TRANSIT_TIMEOUT seconds.
 
